	(text "SPI NOR PY25Q128HA: 16 MB blackbox on SPI0 (U13 C65 R50)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dfdfc503-9aae-5738-91a5-a464359db22e")
	)
	(text_box "Placement (P5): beside the RP2354A on SPI0 (bom_plan region nor, top; either side works). U13, SPI0 and FLASH_CS stay >= 3 mm from the RX antenna hole (spec 4.9 and 11, DRU 'SPI0 3 mm from the RX antenna hole'): SPI0 harmonics fall in the ELRS band, V7 measures desense while logging. C65 at pin 8. Filled+capped 0.35/0.20 via-in-pad allowed in the lead lands, never in the tabs. Betaflight sets SCK to fast slew (bus_spi_pico.c); MOSI and CS keep the reset 4 mA drive and slow slew (EMI lever without parts).\nSourcing: no LCSC listing; NextPCB buys by MPN (D60), the quote confirms it. Same-pinout fallbacks in the Betaflight table (USON-8 4x4 land not staged): PY25Q128HA-QVH-IR, GD25Q128EQIGR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 90.17 0)
		(size 76.2 44.45)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "01ce9a0d-41ce-570b-9418-94a5b1f85e88")
	)
	(text_box "Source: OpenFC-Lite-Mini hardware/blackbox.kicad_sch (rev2). Kept: layout, the 10k CS pull-up (R39 -> R50) and the 100n supply cap (C43 -> C65). Changed: its microSD (Card1) became this 16 MB SPI NOR (D66); the SPI0{SCK,MOSI,MISO} bus label became four hierarchical labels (sch_contract.json).\n\nU13 Puya PY25Q128HA-DFH-IR: 128 Mbit, USON-8 3x3 (DF), 2.7-3.6 V, -40..85 C, fC 133 MHz, READ 03h 80 MHz. JEDEC ID 85 20 18 is in the Betaflight m25p16 table: USE_FLASH_M25P16, SPI0 PA18/PA19/PA20, FLASH_CS_PIN PA21 (PINMAP). SPI0 runs at 75 MHz for writes AND reads: Betaflight bus_spi_pico.c spiCalculateDivider() uses an even prescale >= 2 on clk_peri 150 MHz, so the table's 133 / 80 MHz both give 150/2. Writes are inside fC; reads are not guaranteed: tCLQV 6-7 ns vs the 6.67 ns SCK half period plus pad and trace delay (the RP2350 DS gives no SPI receive timing). Gate F7 / V9: erase, write, read back and CRC a full log, status polling under load; fallback = a lower read clock for this JEDEC ID (firmware cap or table entry), upstreamed with the board config.\n\nWP# (3) and HOLD#/RESET# (7) tied to +3V3: the DS gives an internal pull-up only to the SOP-16 dedicated RESET#, so pin 7 must not float. Delivered SR = 00h, CR = 00h (QE 0, HOLD# function, WPS 0: no block lock) and Betaflight sends 1-bit SPI commands only, so IO2/IO3 never drive against the rail (the ERC pin_to_pin warning on pins 3/7 against a +3V3 power output is this deliberate tie).\n\nR50 10k: CS# must follow VCC at power-up (DS 5.5). RP2354A pads reset with the pull-down on (PDE 1, RPD 36-113 kOhm at 3.3 V): CS >= 36/46 VCC = 0.78 VCC > VIH 0.7 VCC, so U13 stays deselected through reset and boot. U13 and the RP2354A IOVDD share +3V3: no pin above VCC + 0.5 V.\n\nC65 100 nF X6S at pin 8, GND return straight to pin 4 (ICC max 13 mA read, 12 mA erase; adds 0.1 uF nominal to the +3V3 COUT sum of P4-12). EP (9) = two tie-bar tabs with no electrical function in the DS: no-connect, no vias in the tabs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.11 21.59 0)
		(size 78.74 80.01)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
